From: Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>
Subject: doc: resolve mainpage.md against the source directory

doc/Doxyfile.in sets USE_MDFILE_AS_MAINPAGE to a bare relative path, so
an out-of-source build fails: doxygen runs with the build directory as
its working directory (and the generated Doxyfile lives there too),
where mainpage.md does not exist. This used to be a mere warning, but
upstream turned doxygen warnings into errors (commit 32165009), so the
doc build now aborts with "Specified markdown mainpage 'mainpage.md'
does not exist". Point it at the real file.

--- a/doc/Doxyfile.in
+++ b/doc/Doxyfile.in
@@ -930,7 +930,7 @@
 # (index.html). This can be useful if you have a project on for instance GitHub
 # and want to reuse the introduction page also for the doxygen output.

-USE_MDFILE_AS_MAINPAGE = mainpage.md
+USE_MDFILE_AS_MAINPAGE = @CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR@/doc/mainpage.md

 #---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Configuration options related to source browsing
